    <desc>Open or copy web addresses, email addresses and links in the output.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Hyperlinks and email addresses</title>

<p><app>Pano Terminal</app> detects web addresses, email addresses and
  phone numbers in the output, and underlines them when you point at them.
  Programs can also print text that links somewhere, like a link on a web
  page.</p>

  <p>Hold down <key>Ctrl</key> and click a link to open it, or right-click it
  and select:</p>

  <terms>
    <item>
      <title><gui style="menuitem">Open Link</gui> and
      <gui style="menuitem">Copy Link</gui></title>
      <p>Open a web address in your web browser, or copy it to the
      clipboard.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><gui style="menuitem">Send Mail To…</gui> and
      <gui style="menuitem">Copy Mail Address</gui></title>
      <p>Write to an email address with your email application, or copy
      it.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><gui style="menuitem">Call To…</gui> and
      <gui style="menuitem">Copy Call Address</gui></title>
      <p>Call a phone number or a <sys>tel:</sys> or <sys>sip:</sys> address,
      or copy it.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><gui style="menuitem">Open Hyperlink</gui> and
      <gui style="menuitem">Copy Hyperlink Address</gui></title>
      <p>Open or copy the target of text that a program has made a link, for
      example the file names that <cmd>ls --hyperlink</cmd> prints.</p>
    </item>
  </terms>

  <p>To open or copy addresses without the mouse, see
  <link xref="txt-quick-select"/>.</p>

